6 Larch Grove is not in a conservation area. The constraints check also shows it is not a listed building and has no tree preservation order.

Our guidance on windows says that replacement windows in a conservation area need an application unless they match the existing in material and pattern. Since this property isn't in a conservation area, that specific requirement doesn't apply to your proposal.

This is not a formal planning opinion. Whether you need an application for the window work depends on the full details of your proposal, so I'd recommend checking with the council's planning desk before you start, particularly if the replacements differ from the existing windows in any way.
